(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The full C API's layouts (queue 269; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 269\"; 262's DECISION (a), the user"] [4 1 "// 2026-11-10, and 268's DECISION (a), 2026-11-11). Without Py_LIMITED_API, CPython 3.14.10's Include/ reads objects in"] [5 1 "// place: Py_TYPE(o)->tp_flags (PyTuple_Check and the other subclass checks), PyList_Type.tp_new, PyTuple_GET_ITEM's"] [6 1 "// ob_item, PyList_GET_ITEM's ob_item array, PyBytes_AS_STRING's ob_sval, PyFloat_AS_DOUBLE's ob_fval. So:"] [7 1 "//"] [8 1 "//   - a type's handle is a PyTypeObject (PyHeapTypeObject's 936 bytes, or the world's static struct of a type"] [9 1 "//     Include/ names) filled as CPython's: tp_name, the sizes, tp_flags, tp_base, tp_bases, tp_mro, tp_dict, and its"] [10 1 "//     function slots (a type made from a spec its C functions, a pyi type the natives of the generic protocol);"] [11 1 "//   - a tuple's, list's, bytes' and float's handle is a mirror: the object's CPython layout in the world's memory,"] [12 1 "//     made when C first sees the object and kept in step with the pyi value at the C boundary, both ways (as PyPy's"] [13 1 "//     cpyext does): from Go to C before the world is called and when a native returns (the objects it touched), from"] [14 1 "//     C to Go when the world returns and when a native receives a mirrored object (its first use in the native). A"] [15 1 "//     container's mirror holds references to its items' handles, as CPython's container holds its items: a slot C"] [16 1 "//     writes (PyTuple_SET_ITEM, PyList_SET_ITEM) steals the reference C gave, a slot Go changes holds a new one and"] [17 1 "//     gives the old one back, and a mirror released gives its items back."] [18 1 "//"] [19 1 "// Layouts from Include/cpython/{object,tupleobject,listobject,bytesobject,floatobject}.h (CPython 3.14.10, LP64; the"] [20 1 "// PSF's license, LICENSE.md); the slots' offsets are Objects/typeslots.inc's."] [36 1 "// PyTypeObject's and PyHeapTypeObject's fields (offsets, LP64)"] [38 28 "// sizeof(PyHeapTypeObject)"] [69 1 "// slotOffsets is Objects/typeslots.inc (slot id -> the sub-struct's field offset, -1 for none, and the type's field"] [70 1 "// offset), from CPython 3.14.10's headers by gcc (offsetof, LP64)."] [80 1 "// the heap type's own sub-structs (PyHeapTypeObject's as_async, as_number, ...), by the type's field that points"] [81 1 "// at one"] [85 1 "// builtinTpFlags are CPython 3.14.10's tp_flags of the types Include/ names (type.__flags__, python3 3.14.10)."] [101 1 "// typeFlags is t's tp_flags as a C reader sees them: CPython's own for the types Include/ names, a type's made from a"] [102 1 "// spec or by PyType_Ready its own, else the subclass bits, BASETYPE and HEAPTYPE pyi knows, READY, the version tag,"] [103 1 "// IMMUTABLETYPE for a static type, and HAVE_GC for a heap type."] [106 52 "// inherit_special: the base's fast-subclass bits"] [111 2 "// no HAVE_VERSION_TAG: 3.14 keeps the bit for compatibility and sets it on no type (queue 594: test_type_getflags)"] [116 4 "// a class over object alone, with no __slots__: its dict and weak references managed, its values inline, as"] [117 4 "// type_new's add_dict and add_weak and type_ready_managed_dict make them"] [126 1 "// tpInlineValues is Py_TPFLAGS_INLINE_VALUES."] [129 1 "// plainClass is whether t is a class statement's over object alone (every class of its MRO but object a heap class no"] [130 1 "// C type made, none with __slots__)."] [146 1 "// cTpName is tp_name: a C type's own, a heap class's __name__, a static type's module-qualified name outside builtins."] [157 1 "// genericSlots are the natives a pyi type's function slots point at (the generic protocol's functions of the same"] [158 1 "// signature), by slot id: C calling Py_TYPE(o)->tp_repr(o) calls PyObject_Repr."] [164 1 "// fillTypeObject writes t's PyTypeObject at a (its handle: the head is written by the caller; the fields of a"] [165 1 "// PyHeapTypeObject's size, or of a static struct's)."] [195 2 "// the function slots: a C type's own (its spec's or PyType_Ready's, inherited), else the generic natives"] [201 57 "// tp_doc: the spec's copy (queue 270b)"] [203 3 "// ht_name, ht_qualname (queue 270b: test_type_from_ephemeral_spec reads them)"] [206 3 "// ht_module (queue 521: _decimal's find_state_left_or_right reads it in place, pycore_typeobject.h's inline"] [207 3 "// _PyType_GetModuleState), the module PyType_FromModuleAndSpec named, kept for the process as the type is"] [252 1 "// classNew reports whether t's __new__ is a class statement's (the first dictionary of its MRO holding __new__ is a"] [253 1 "// pyi class's, not a built-in's or a C type's): its tp_new is then CPython's slot_tp_new (Objects/typeobject.c,"] [254 1 "// type_new's tp_new for a class whose namespace defines __new__, which its subclasses inherit), the class's __new__"] [255 1 "// called, not its built-in base's (_pickle's load_newobj calls cls->tp_new: a list or tuple subclass's __new__,"] [256 1 "// test_descr's test_reduce_copying, a NamedTuple's, test_enum's tuple subclasses)."] [269 1 "// storeSlot writes the function fn into the slot id of the type object at a (its sub-struct's field when the type"] [270 1 "// has that sub-struct)."] [283 1 "// loadSlot reads the slot id of the type object at a (0: none, or no sub-struct)."] [296 1 "// ---- mirrors ----"] [298 1 "// mirror is the CPython layout of a tuple, list, bytes, float, int or str in the world's memory, a handle's."] [300 17 "// 't' tuple, 'l' list, 'b' bytes, 'f' float, 'i' int, 'u' str"] [301 17 "// the pyi object (a subclass's instance too: its built-in part is mirrored)"] [302 17 "// a tuple's or list's slots as last synchronized"] [303 17 "// a bytes' contents as last synchronized"] [304 17 "// the synchronization epoch of the last copy from C"] [305 2 "// a str's (queue 270, capi_unicode.go): its kind, ASCII flag and characters' address; a str PyUnicode_New made"] [306 2