em does not overwrite it (queue 597: _elementtree's treebuilder_handle_data"] [514 3 "// fills a PyList_New(2) by PyList_SET_ITEM, then a C type's call from Python code its comment factory ran wrote"] [515 3 "// every mirror to C, the stale nil items over C's: test_late_tail_mix_pi_comments' Go panic)"] [516 3 "// The slot so taken holds C's own reference (PyList_SET_ITEM steals it), not one of the mirror's: it is the slot's"] [517 3 "// synchronized value from now on, so the loop below neither writes it nor holds a reference of the mirror's on it"] [518 3 "// (which nothing would give back: the item would live as long as the process, py-pickle-heap-1126); the slot's"] [519 3 "// earlier item is given back as an item Go replaced is"] [558 1 "// syncFromC copies what C wrote into its mirror to the pyi value (the slots C changed; a NULL slot is a nil item, as"] [559 1 "// CPython's NULL until C fills it), and does so for the mirrors its items name, once an epoch."] [588 3 "// C's slots as last synchronized: C changed nothing, so Go's value stands (Python code a native ran may have"] [589 3 "// resized the list since: gh-72054's __index__ popping from it, test_slice's getindicesex_seq), written to C"] [590 3 "// when the native that uses it returns"] [622 10 "// resized from C: not provided (PyByteArray_Resize is a native)"] [645 1 "// holdRef and unholdRef are a mirror's reference to an item Go put in it, and its giving back."] [665 1 "// cOnly reports whether C holds the only reference to the handle h (its count, less the mirrors' own, is 1)."] [668 1 "// rawObj is the object a handle names without synchronizing it (nil for NULL)."] [677 1 "// freeMirror releases a mirror's own memory and its items' references (its handle released)."] [697 1 "// syncAllToC writes every mirror's pyi state into C (before the world is called: Python code may have changed any)."] [704 1 "// syncUsedLists writes to C the lists' mirrors the natives used since the outermost entry into the world (usedLists)"] [705 1 "// whose length Python code changed, C's own writes taken first: a native that ran Python code returns (that code may have"] [706 1 "// resized a list C reads in place, PyList_GET_SIZE's ob_size: gh-92930's persistent_id clearing the list _pickle's"] [707 1 "// batch_list_exact walks, test_pickle's test_evil_pickler_mutating_collection, \"list changed size during iteration\")."] [711 25 "// released since"] [721 1 "// usedLists are the lists' mirrors natives used (touch) since the outermost entry into the world (World.Call, worldDepth"] [722 1 "// its nesting)."] [728 1 "// syncAllFromC copies every mirror's C state to its pyi value (when the world returns to Python)."] [736 1 "// nativeEnter and nativeLeave bracket a native's (or a closure's) run: what C wrote is copied to Go on the first use"] [737 1 "// of a mirrored object in it (fromHandle), and the mirrors it used are written back to C when it returns."] [758 1 "// touch marks a mirrored handle as used by the running native."] [770 1 "// ---- C types over a built-in base (268's DECISION (a), the user 2026-11-11) ----"] [772 1 "// born is a C type's instance over a built-in base (a type a spec or PyType_Ready made, deriving from list, tuple,"] [773 1 "// bytes or float): its memory is the world's, tp_basicsize bytes (and its items'), the built-in part a mirror of the"] [774 1 "// pyi value at its head, the extension's part C's after the base's size. The Go value is an instance of the type"] [775 1 "// keeping a built-in value, as a Python class deriving from the built-in keeps one; the record rides on it"] [776 1 "// (py.SetInstanceExt). Its memory lives as a C-born object's (queue 268): until Go collects the instance, then its"] [777 1 "// tp_dealloc runs on the world's next entry."] [785 1 "// bornKind is the mirrored layout of t's built-in base (0: none of them)."] [798 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over int (its mirror a PyLongObject's)"] [801 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over an exception (no mirror: C reads its fields through functions)"] [807 1 "// bornOf is o's record when o is a C type's instance over a built-in base (nil: none)."] [819 1 "// bornHandle is such an instance's handle: its memory's address, in the maps again (a count of 0: unowned until the"] [820 1 "// C entry ends; its mirror written from Go, which may have changed it meanwhile) when it had left them."] [837 1 "// bornNew is tp_alloc for a C type over a built-in base: the instance of sub with nitems items (a tuple's or bytes'),"] [838 1 "// a new reference."] [865 1 "// bornValue is the built-in value of a C type's instance over a built-in base its base's __new__ makes from the"] [866 1 "// arguments (queue 270b: a spec over int without tp_new, HeapCTypeWithBasesSlot(5)): the base's own value, or for an"] [867 1 "// exception the exception of sub itself."] [887 1 "// bornWith makes the instance of sub keeping the built-in value v (for an exception, v is the instance), its memory"] [888 1 "// the world's: tp_basicsize bytes (and nitems items') or the mirror's size, the built-in part mirrored."] [937 1 "// allocObj is tp_alloc's generic allocation of t (PyType_GenericAlloc): a C-born object, an instance over a built-in"] [938 1 "// base, or a type object's memory (type's own tp_alloc: a heap type C fills, then PyType_Ready's)."] [941 3 "// a type object (a C metaclass's too, queue 270b: its basicsize, the C tail after the PyHeapTypeObject)"] [962 3 "// a built-in type of pyi's whose zero value is an instance (queue 594: _io._BytesIOBuffer's tp_alloc in"] [963 3 "// test_pep3118_obsolete_write_locks): a new reference"] [975 1 "// rawTypes are the type objects C allocated through type's tp_alloc, not ready yet."] [978 1 "// bornDealloc is a built-in base's tp_dealloc on a C instance's memory (list_dealloc, tupledealloc ...): its items'"] [979 1 "// references given back as CPython's do, read from its memory, the list's array and the memory freed."] [1001 1 "// ---- PyType_Ready for